Decided: cooee update runs the embedded scripts/install.sh with COOEE_REV=<sha>, so the install and codesign steps exist once
Because: "It installs with the same steps as `install.sh`"
Decided: the old binary is kept as ~/.cargo/bin/cooee.old and renamed back when the restarted service doesn't answer
Because: "If that check fails, it puts back the previous binary and restarts it."
Decided: a sha that failed is written to update.failed and not retried, so a broken green head doesn't restart the service every 15 minutes
Decided: the timer is a LaunchAgent with a fixed label built by the same plist() as the service, so a second setup skips it
Because: crates/cooee/src/setup.rs:112
Rejected: a systemd user timer — setup installs and restarts the service only through launchctl, so Linux has no cooee service to restart
